evious Slide\nNext Slide\nExceptional Cardiology Care for Dogs and Cats in Dallas – Ft. Worth\nYour pet is a part of your family, and we understand that facing a medical difficulty can be stressful. You can rely on our compassionate, expert team to make the process as easy as possible, and you’ll get updates each step of the way to put your mind at ease.\nMedVet Grapevine serves as an extension of your family veterinarian should your pet need specialty veterinary care. Our team has the expertise and the resources in our state-of-the-art facility to diagnose and treat your pet for a healthy heart and lungs. We value open communication with you and your family veterinarian so we can all partner together to provide the best care for your pet so they can have a longer, more active life.\nMedVet Grapevine Caregivers\nSearch by Name\nFilter by Specialty\nAll Specialties\nCardiology\nOur Hospital Leaders\nCarrie Davis, DVM, DACVAA\nMedical Director\nKim Ward\nHospital Director\nOur Doctors\nRebecca Fields Bennie\n, DVM, Residency Trained in Cardiology\nCardiology\nPet Stories\n“\nMedVet employees love every animal and are friendly to humans too. The doctor we met is the best! After 2.5 days, we brought our Angel home. They called to check on Angel at home, even on a holiday. Angel is doing well!”\nPrevious Story\nNext Story\nFinancing Options\nWe understand that planning for the cost of care is important. Special financing and payment arrangements are available for qualified pet owners through an independent company, CareCredit.\nLearn More\nFind a location\nEmergency Care\nFind Care\nFind a Location\nFind A Doctor\nResources\nPet Care Resources\nClinical Studies\nAbout\nWe Are MedVet\nMedVet Experience\nOur Leaders\nOur Founders\nNewsroom\nDiversity, Inclusion, & Belonging\nCommunity Support\nFAQs\nContact Us\nFor Veterinarians\nClinical Studies\nContinuing Education\nCareers\nMedVet Open Positions at New Hospitals\nMedVet Training Programs\nSpecialties\nSpecialties Overv